                <pb facs="0396" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg308"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay instructs Mr. Porter to convey to the minister for foreign affairs the
                    deep appreciation of the President of the kindly and efficient cooperation of
                    the French Government in effecting the rescue of Mr. Perdicaris.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
